      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 100,
          "username": "ShanShanTukBoi",
          "title": "Kazakhstan to Kyrgyzstan",
          "text": "Our bus from Almaty to Karakol broke down just outside of Almaty. After waiting 90 minutes on the side of the highway in 37-degree heat for a replacement bus to arrive, the new bus immediately broke down in the same place, seemingly with the same issue. After another hour of the two bus drivers (and several passengers) fiddling around with the engine, we were on the road again. There were a few more breakdowns along the way, but we eventually made it through the border crossing and arrived in Karakol after around 11 hours on the road (it should have been ~5 hours).",
          "photos": [
            "https://imgur.com/rFZc8oL.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/hEqPSES.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/ZtVLPlk.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/PRxx1eL.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/Sy29siZ.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/lB0LUgn.jpeg"
          ],
          "date": "2026-08-17T06:06:38Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "username": "graciemq",
          "title": "Trapped in Karakol",
          "text": "**Grace\u2019s corner** Rushan and me have both been unwell, which means we have spent 5 days in Karakol. Don\u2019t get me wrong, it is a nice little town but is mainly used as a base for hiking with limited sights to see. As such, we wake up everyday, don\u2019t feel well enough and book another night here. \n\nWe also celebrated 8 years together and went to a hot spring (not pictured) \ud83e\udd73",
          "photos": [
            "https://imgur.com/XvOsJw1.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/qrqv5GO.jpeg"
          ],
          "date": "2026-08-21T11:28:23Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "username": "graciemq",
          "title": "Hiking to Ala-Kul lake",
          "text": "**Grace\u2019s corner** After two days of hiking I am feeling grubby, sore and grateful. Day 1 was hiking from Karakol Gorge to Sirota Yurt Camp (14km, 900m elevation gain). Day 2 was hiking past the very aqua Ala-Kul lake to Altyn-Arashan (18km, 1300m elevation gain). Day 2 we got to just shy of 4000m altitude and hiked for ten hours (I got a bit grumpy - sorry Rushan!). I am very keen for a hot meal and shower tonight :)",
          "photos": [
            "https://imgur.com/894axOX.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/zbCvYQW.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/Yv6iutG.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/8DeX6mj.jpeg",
            "https://imgur.com/Aw2QLoe.jpeg"
