          "title": "Off-roading in a loaf of bread",
          "text": "We were supposed to spend a third day hiking back to the road, but storms overnight turned the track into thick mud. So, we ended up splitting an off-road taxi with some people from our yurt camp. The local drivers use old Soviet 4x4 vehicles to manage the terrain. The UAZ we rode in is known as a Bukhanka (\u201cloaf of bread\u201d) in Russian. The drive took over two hours even though the distance was only around 16 km.",
